<section>
  <h2>PNG, HEIC and WebP photos</h2>
  <p>The container differs. The cleaning step does not.</p>
  <h3>PNG</h3>
  <p>
    PNG files often carry text chunks. Stable Diffusion and ComfyUI store prompts and workflow settings
    there as plain text. The tool removes those chunks and the EXIF chunk; the color profile and image
    data stay. For PNG, removing metadata is a chunk-level operation, and the image pixels are untouched.
  </p>
  <h3>HEIC</h3>
  <p>
    iPhones often shoot HEIC. The cleaner works on the file's box structure, removes the EXIF and XMP
    items and rebuilds the box sizes. HEIC metadata removal needs no re-encoding, and if a field cannot
    be checked, the report says so instead of guessing.
  </p>
  <h3>WebP</h3>
  <p>
    WebP stores EXIF and XMP as separate chunks, with header flags that announce them. The tool removes
    both chunks and clears those flags, so no reader goes looking for metadata that was removed. Image
    and animation chunks are left as they are.
  </p>
</section>
